{%- comment -%} Styles live in assets/ha-sections.css, loaded once in layout/theme.liquid. {%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — THE MASTERS (the /pages/the-masters page).
  Aloha's "The Masters: Build Brief for Ivan" and the founder's
  Hartwick_The_Masters.png (left board: the public page; centre: interaction
  notes; right: expanded glossary copy), 18 September 2026. Confirmed by
  Angela, per Aloha's message the same day.

  The page in reading order, each part a setting or a block so nothing is
  hard-coded (CLAUDE.md: reusable sections, no hard-coded editorial pages):

    hero        the wide loom photograph with a small framed monochrome inset
                overlapping the transition into the introduction
    intro       THE MASTERS (the one H1), THE PEOPLE. THE KNOWLEDGE. THE WORK.,
                and Angela's introduction divided across THE CLOTH / THE
                KNOWLEDGE / THE HANDWORK with her complete wording
    pair        a still on the left, the weaving film on the right; the play
                control belongs to the film and appears only when a film exists
    archive     three small archival images and the Gandhi quotation
    glossary    eleven techniques as compact ruled rows; one opens at a time
                into its fuller copy, matching media, caption and credit
    feature     the wide archive film, "At the printing table."
    continue    THE WORK CONTINUES and the Journal link
    (then the shared Register and footer from the template)

  FILMS. Every film slot is a Shopify video (Files) with an optional poster.
  Playback starts only on the visible Play button: no autoplay, nothing on
  hover or scroll, one film at a time, paused when it leaves view, native
  controls (pause, sound, captions, full screen) once playing. With no video
  attached the slot renders as a still WITHOUT a play control — the brief's
  "stills never masquerade as films". assets/ha-masters.js carries this.

  GLOSSARY. Real buttons with aria-expanded and a labelled region each; Enter
  and Space work natively; visible focus. Every technique has a stable id
  (#khadi, #handwoven …) and a direct link opens that entry. The complete
  text of every entry is in the HTML whether or not its panel is open — the
  panels are collapsed by the script, so search systems and no-JS readers get
  everything. Normal scrolling only; the script never hijacks the scroll.

  SYMBOLS. Aloha, 18 September: "don't use the icons that are in the Masters
  Page. I will be placing something else instead." The positions where the
  artboard puts a symbol are optional image slots, empty by default.

  CONTENT. Copy is transcribed from the two boards. The expanded glossary
  copy is the founder's editorial DRAFT pending Angela's review (brief §3);
  the placeholder notice stays on until Aloha signs it off. Photographs and
  films come from the store's own Files — the matches the store can honestly
  make — until the Masters edits from Angela's folder are uploaded. No artisan
  name, location or credit is invented: the credit and Master fields exist
  and render only once they are filled.

  LATER (brief §7): individual Master records. Each technique carries a
  hidden record ID and a separate, optional destination link, so Master
  profiles or the future Made by Masters site connect without a rebuild.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign hero = section.settings.hero_image
  assign hero_paper = section.settings.hero_paper
  assign hero_focus = '--ha-mst-focus: ' | append: section.settings.hero_focus_x | append: '% ' | append: section.settings.hero_focus_y | append: '%'
  assign inset = section.settings.inset_image
  assign still = section.settings.still_image
  assign still_focus = '--ha-mst-focus: ' | append: section.settings.still_focus_x | append: '% ' | append: section.settings.still_focus_y | append: '%'
  assign film_focus = '--ha-mst-focus: ' | append: section.settings.film_focus_x | append: '% ' | append: section.settings.film_focus_y | append: '%'
  assign feature_focus = '--ha-mst-focus: ' | append: section.settings.feature_focus_x | append: '% ' | append: section.settings.feature_focus_y | append: '%'
  assign transcript_label = section.settings.transcript_label | default: 'Transcript'
  assign empty_text = section.settings.empty_text | default: 'To supply'
  assign ink = section.settings.ink
-%}
<script>document.documentElement.classList.add('ha-mst-js');</script>
<script src="{{ 'ha-masters.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

<div class="ha-mst ha-mst--ink-{{ ink }}" id="the-masters" data-mst data-mst-muted="{{ section.settings.start_muted }}">
  {%- capture p_hero -%}
  {%- comment -%} ---------- HERO: the wide photograph, the framed inset ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <header class="ha-mst__hero{% if inset %} ha-mst__hero--inset{% endif %}">
    {%- comment -%} Aloha, 25 September 2026: the header is her yellow paper (b2aa72) alone, no photograph; the menu is transparent over it (header setting "Transparent on these pages"). {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if hero_paper -%}
    <figure class="ha-mst__hero-figure ha-mst__hero-figure--paper ha-figure ha-grain-block ha-grain-block--over" style="--ha-mst-paper: url('{{ hero_paper | image_url: width: 2800 }}')">
    {%- else -%}
    <figure class="ha-mst__hero-figure ha-figure ha-grain-block ha-grain-block--over{% unless hero %} ha-figure--empty{% endunless %}">
    {%- endif -%}
      {%- if hero_paper -%}
      {%- elsif hero -%}
        {{ hero | image_url: width: 2800 | image_tag: loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high', sizes: '100vw', widths: '750, 1100, 1500, 2000, 2800', alt: section.settings.hero_alt, class: 'ha-mst__hero-img', style: hero_focus }}
      {%- else -%}
        <span class="ha-mst__empty ha-record">{{ empty_text }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.hero_label != blank -%}
        <figcaption class="ha-mst__hero-label ha-record">{{ section.settings.hero_label }}</figcaption>
      {%- endif -%}
    </figure>
    {%- if inset -%}
      <figure class="ha-mst__inset">
        {{ inset | image_url: width: 800 | image_tag: loading: 'eager', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 15vw, 40vw', widths: '240, 320, 400, 600, 800', alt: section.settings.inset_alt, class: 'ha-mst__inset-img' }}
      </figure>
    {%- endif -%}
  </header>
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- capture p_intro -%}
  {%- comment -%} ---------- INTRODUCTION: one H1, the line, three columns ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ha-section ha-mst__intro" aria-labelledby="ha-mst-title">
    <div class="ha-wrap ha-mst__intro-inner">
      <h1 id="ha-mst-title" class="ha-mst__title ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h1>
      {%- if section.settings.subline != blank -%}
        <p class="ha-mst__subline ha-identify">{{ section.settings.subline }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <div class="ha-mst__columns">
        {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
          {%- assign k_label = 'col' | append: i | append: '_label' -%}
          {%- assign k_body = 'col' | append: i | append: '_body' -%}
          {%- assign k_symbol = 'col' | append: i | append: '_symbol' -%}
          {%- assign col_symbol = section.settings[k_symbol] -%}
          {%- if section.settings[k_body] != blank -%}
            <div class="ha-mst__col{% if col_symbol %} ha-mst__col--symbol{% endif %}">
              <div class="ha-mst__col-text">
                {%- if section.settings[k_label] != blank -%}<h2 class="ha-mst__col-label ha-record">{{ section.settings[k_label] }}</h2>{%- endif -%}
                <div class="ha-mst__col-body ha-narrate">{{ section.settings[k_body] }}</div>
              </div>
              {%- if col_symbol -%}
                {%- comment -%} A decorative symbol: empty alt, never a control. {%- endcomment -%}
                <figure class="ha-mst__symbol">{{ col_symbol | image_url: width: 240 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '80px', widths: '80, 160, 240', alt: '' }}</figure>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- capture p_pair -%}
  {%- comment -%} ---------- STILL AND MOVEMENT ----------
    Two figures. On a phone each caption sits under its own image; from 750px
    the figures become `display: contents` so the two frames share one row
    and the two captions the row beneath, as the artboard draws them.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ha-mst__pair" aria-label="{{ section.settings.pair_aria | default: 'Still and movement' }}">
    <div class="ha-mst__pair-grid">
      <figure class="ha-mst__still">
        <div class="ha-mst__still-frame ha-figure{% unless still %} ha-figure--empty{% endunless %}">
          {%- if still -%}
            {{ still | image_url: width: 1600 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 50vw, 100vw', widths: '600, 900, 1200, 1600', alt: section.settings.still_alt, class: 'ha-mst__still-img', style: still_focus }}
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="ha-mst__empty ha-record">{{ empty_text }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <figcaption class="ha-mst__caption ha-mst__caption--still">
          {%- if section.settings.still_number != blank -%}<span class="ha-mst__caption-num ha-record">{{ section.settings.still_number }}</span>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.still_caption != blank -%}<span class="ha-mst__caption-text ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.still_caption }}</span>{%- endif -%}
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="ha-mst__movement">
        {%- render 'ha-masters-film',
          variant: 'panel',
          id: 'ha-mst-film-weaving',
          video: section.settings.film_video,
          poster: section.settings.film_poster,
          poster_alt: section.settings.film_poster_alt,
          focus: film_focus,
          label: section.settings.film_label,
          sublabel: section.settings.film_sublabel,
          title: section.settings.film_title,
          transcript: section.settings.film_transcript,
          transcript_label: transcript_label,
          captions_url: section.settings.film_captions,
          credit: section.settings.film_credit,
          date: section.settings.film_date,
          empty_text: empty_text,
          sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 50vw, 100vw'
        -%}
        <figcaption class="ha-mst__caption ha-mst__caption--film">
          {%- if section.settings.film_number != blank -%}<span class="ha-mst__caption-num ha-record">{{ section.settings.film_number }}</span>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.film_caption != blank -%}<span class="ha-mst__caption-text ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.film_caption }}</span>{%- endif -%}
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- capture p_archive -%}
  {%- comment -%} ---------- ARCHIVE TILES AND THE QUOTATION ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ha-section ha-mst__archive" aria-labelledby="ha-mst-quote-label">
    <div class="ha-wrap ha-mst__archive-inner">
      {%- assign tiles = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'archive' -%}
      {%- if tiles.size > 0 -%}
        <ul class="ha-mst__tiles" role="list">
          {%- for tile in tiles -%}
            <li class="ha-mst__tile" {{ tile.shopify_attributes }}>
              {%- render 'ha-masters-film',
                variant: 'tile',
                id: tile.id,
                video: tile.settings.video,
                poster: tile.settings.image,
                poster_alt: tile.settings.alt,
                title: tile.settings.title,
                transcript: tile.settings.transcript,
                transcript_label: transcript_label,
                captions_url: tile.settings.captions,
                credit: tile.settings.credit,
                date: tile.settings.date,
                empty_text: empty_text,
                sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 12vw, 30vw'
              -%}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}
      <p id="ha-mst-quote-label" class="ha-mst__quote-label ha-record">{{ section.settings.quote_label }}</p>
      <blockquote class="ha-mst__quote">
        <p class="ha-mst__quote-text ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.quote | newline_to_br }}</p>
        {%- if section.settings.quote_cite != blank -%}<footer class="ha-mst__quote-cite ha-record">{{ section.settings.quote_cite }}</footer>{%- endif -%}
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- capture p_glossary -%}
  {%- comment -%} ---------- THE GLOSSARY OF HERITAGE TECHNIQUES ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ha-section ha-mst__glossary" id="glossary" aria-labelledby="ha-mst-glossary-title">
    <div class="ha-wrap">
      <div class="ha-mst__glossary-head">
        <h2 id="ha-mst-glossary-title" class="ha-mst__glossary-title ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.glossary_heading | newline_to_br }}</h2>
        <div class="ha-mst__glossary-lead{% if section.settings.glossary_symbol %} ha-mst__glossary-lead--symbol{% endif %}">
          {%- if section.settings.glossary_symbol -%}
            <figure class="ha-mst__symbol">{{ section.settings.glossary_symbol | image_url: width: 240 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '80px', widths: '80, 160, 240', alt: '' }}</figure>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.glossary_intro != blank -%}<p class="ha-mst__glossary-intro ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.glossary_intro }}</p>{%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>

      <ol class="ha-mst__list" role="list">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- if block.type == 'technique' -%}
            {%- assign key = block.settings.key | default: block.settings.title | handleize -%}
            {%- assign has_link = false -%}
            {%- if block.settings.master_url != blank and block.settings.master_text != blank -%}{%- assign has_link = true -%}{%- endif -%}
            <li class="ha-mst__row" id="{{ key }}" data-mst-row {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <h3 class="ha-mst__row-head">
                <button type="button" class="ha-mst__toggle" id="{{ key }}-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="{{ key }}-panel" data-mst-toggle data-mst-key="{{ key }}">
                  <span class="ha-mst__row-num ha-record">{{ block.settings.number }}</span>
                  <span class="ha-mst__row-title ha-narrate">{{ block.settings.title }}</span>
                  {%- if block.settings.summary != blank -%}<span class="ha-mst__row-summary ha-narrate">{{ block.settings.summary }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                  <span class="ha-mst__row-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                </button>
              </h3>
              <div class="ha-mst__panel" id="{{ key }}-panel" role="region" aria-labelledby="{{ key }}-toggle" data-mst-panel>
                <button type="button" class="ha-mst__close ha-record" data-mst-close>{{ section.settings.close_text | default: 'Close' }}</button>
                {%- assign has_media = false -%}
                {%- if block.settings.video != blank or block.settings.image != blank -%}{%- assign has_media = true -%}{%- endif -%}
                <div class="ha-mst__panel-grid{% unless has_media %} ha-mst__panel-grid--text{% endunless %}">
                  {%- if has_media -%}
                    <div class="ha-mst__panel-media">
                      {%- render 'ha-masters-film',
                        variant: 'glossary',
                        id: key,
                        video: block.settings.video,
                        poster: block.settings.image,
                        poster_alt: block.settings.alt,
                        title: block.settings.film_title,
                        transcript: block.settings.transcript,
                        transcript_label: transcript_label,
                        captions_url: block.settings.captions,
                        credit: block.settings.credit,
                        date: block.settings.date,
                        empty_text: empty_text,
                        sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 34vw, 100vw'
                      -%}
                      {%- if block.settings.caption != blank -%}<p class="ha-mst__panel-caption ha-record">{{ block.settings.caption }}</p>{%- endif -%}
                    </div>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <div class="ha-mst__panel-text">
                    {%- if block.settings.tagline != blank -%}<p class="ha-mst__panel-eyebrow ha-record">{{ block.settings.tagline }}</p>{%- endif -%}
                    <div class="ha-mst__panel-body ha-narrate">{{ block.settings.body }}</div>
                    {%- if block.settings.credit != blank -%}
                      <p class="ha-mst__panel-credit ha-record"><span class="ha-mst__panel-credit-label">{{ section.settings.credit_label }}</span> {{ block.settings.credit }}</p>
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {%- if has_link -%}
                      <a class="ha-mst__panel-link ha-record" href="{{ block.settings.master_url }}"{% if block.settings.master_id != blank %} data-master-id="{{ block.settings.master_id | escape }}"{% endif %}>{{ block.settings.master_text }}<span class="ha-mst__corner" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ol>

      {%- if section.settings.handwork_line != blank -%}
        <div class="ha-mst__handwork">
          {%- if section.settings.handwork_label != blank -%}<p class="ha-mst__handwork-label ha-record">{{ section.settings.handwork_label }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          <p class="ha-mst__handwork-line ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.handwork_line }}</p>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- capture p_feature -%}
  {%- comment -%} ---------- FROM THE HARTWICK ARCHIVE: the wide film ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ha-mst__feature" aria-label="{{ section.settings.feature_title | escape }}">
    {%- render 'ha-masters-film',
      variant: 'feature',
      id: 'ha-mst-film-feature',
      video: section.settings.feature_video,
      poster: section.settings.feature_poster,
      poster_alt: section.settings.feature_poster_alt,
      focus: feature_focus,
      eyebrow: section.settings.feature_eyebrow,
      label: section.settings.feature_title,
      sublabel: section.settings.feature_sublabel,
      title: section.settings.feature_title,
      transcript: section.settings.feature_transcript,
      transcript_label: transcript_label,
      captions_url: section.settings.feature_captions,
      credit: section.settings.feature_credit,
      date: section.settings.feature_date,
      monochrome: section.settings.feature_mono,
      empty_text: empty_text,
      sizes: '100vw'
    -%}
  </section>
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- capture p_continue -%}
  {%- comment -%} ---------- THE WORK CONTINUES ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ha-section ha-mst__continue" aria-labelledby="ha-mst-continue-title">
    <div class="ha-wrap ha-mst__continue-grid{% if section.settings.continue_image %} ha-mst__continue-grid--image{% endif %}">
      <h2 id="ha-mst-continue-title" class="ha-mst__continue-heading ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.continue_heading }}</h2>
      {%- if section.settings.continue_image -%}
        <figure class="ha-mst__continue-figure">{{ section.settings.continue_image | image_url: width: 480 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 12vw, 40vw', widths: '160, 240, 320, 480', alt: section.settings.continue_alt }}</figure>
      {%- endif -%}
      <div class="ha-mst__continue-text">
        {%- if section.settings.continue_body != blank -%}<div class="ha-body ha-narrate ha-mst__continue-body">{{ section.settings.continue_body }}</div>{%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.continue_link_text != blank -%}
          <a class="ha-mst__continue-link ha-record" href="{{ section.settings.continue_link_url | default: '/blogs/news' }}" data-mst-journal>{{ section.settings.continue_link_text }}<span class="ha-mst__corner" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ha-wrap ha-mst__note-wrap">
      {%- render 'ha-placeholder-note', show: section.settings.show_placeholder_note, text: section.settings.placeholder_text -%}
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- comment -%} ========== 26 SEPTEMBER 2026 — Aloha's new order ==========
    Her Masters board (Temp Files/MASTERS.pdf) rearranged the page from
    screenshots of the site: the yellow paper opening now carries the khadi
    quotation and MADE BY MASTERS; beneath the first ring bar, THE KNOWLEDGE
    BEHIND THE WORK (the three columns, each with a dye swatch, a swatch
    hanging from the rings) and her collage beside three paragraphs; a plain
    bar; the glossary; a ring bar straight onto the still and the film; the
    printing table; The work continues. The three small archive tiles are not
    on her board (Layout: 18 September brings them back).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture p_hero26 -%}
  <header class="ha-mst__hero ha-mst__hero--sep26">
    <div class="ha-mst__hero-figure ha-mst__hero-figure--paper ha-mst__hero26 ha-page-grain ha-grain-block"{% if hero_paper %} style="--ha-mst-paper: url('{{ hero_paper | image_url: width: 2800 }}')"{% endif %}>
      <div class="ha-mst__hero26-quote">
        {%- if section.settings.quote_label != blank -%}<p class="ha-mst__hero26-label ha-label">{{ section.settings.quote_label }}</p>{%- endif -%}
        <blockquote class="ha-mst__hero26-bq">
          <p class="ha-mst__hero26-text ha-pull">{{ section.settings.quote | newline_to_br }}</p>
          {%- if section.settings.quote_cite != blank -%}<footer class="ha-mst__hero26-cite ha-label">{{ section.settings.quote_cite }}</footer>{%- endif -%}
        </blockquote>
      </div>
      <div class="ha-mst__hero26-title">
        <h1 id="ha-mst-title" class="ha-mst__hero26-h1 ha-label">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h1>
        {%- if section.settings.subline != blank -%}<p class="ha-mst__hero26-sub ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.subline }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- capture p_rings -%}
  <div class="ha-home-binding-section ha-mst__bar"><div class="ha-home-binding ha-home-binding--rings ha-home-binding--masters ha-page-grain ha-grain-block" aria-hidden="true">
    {%- for i in (1..3) -%}<img class="ha-home-binding__ring ha-home-binding__ring--{{ i }}" src="{{ 'ha-ring-upright.svg' | asset_url }}" width="55" height="290" alt="" loading="lazy">{%- endfor -%}
  </div></div>
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- capture p_bar -%}
  <div class="ha-home-binding-section ha-mst__bar"><div class="ha-home-binding ha-page-grain ha-grain-block" aria-hidden="true"></div></div>
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- capture p_knowledge -%}
  <section class="ha-section ha-mst__knowledge" aria-labelledby="ha-mst-knowledge-title">
    {%- if section.settings.knowledge_spot -%}
      <figure class="ha-mst__knowledge-spot" aria-hidden="true">{{ section.settings.knowledge_spot | image_url: width: 600 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 17vw, 30vw', widths: '300, 450, 600', alt: '' }}</figure>
    {%- endif -%}
    <div class="ha-wrap ha-mst__knowledge-inner">
      <h2 id="ha-mst-knowledge-title" class="ha-mst__knowledge-label ha-label">{{ section.settings.knowledge_label }}</h2>
      <div class="ha-mst__knowledge-cols">
        {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
          {%- assign k_label = 'col' | append: i | append: '_label' -%}
          {%- assign k_body = 'col' | append: i | append: '_body' -%}
          {%- assign k_symbol = 'col' | append: i | append: '_symbol' -%}
          {%- if section.settings[k_body] != blank -%}
            <div class="ha-mst__kcol ha-mst__kcol--{{ i }}">
              {%- if section.settings[k_label] != blank -%}<h3 class="ha-mst__kcol-label ha-narrate">{{ section.settings[k_label] }}</h3>{%- endif -%}
              <div class="ha-mst__kcol-body ha-narrate">{{ section.settings[k_body] }}</div>
              {%- if section.settings[k_symbol] -%}
                <figure class="ha-mst__kcol-spot" aria-hidden="true">{{ section.settings[k_symbol] | image_url: width: 480 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 16vw, 40vw', widths: '240, 360, 480', alt: '' }}</figure>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
      {%- if section.settings.story_image or section.settings.story_body != blank -%}
        <div class="ha-mst__story">
          {%- if section.settings.story_image -%}
            <figure class="ha-mst__story-figure">{{ section.settings.story_image | image_url: width: 1200 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 37vw, 90vw', widths: '600, 900, 1200', alt: section.settings.story_alt, class: 'ha-mst__story-img' }}</figure>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.story_body != blank -%}
            <div class="ha-mst__story-body ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.story_body }}</div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- if section.settings.layout == 'sep26' -%}
    {{ p_hero26 }}{{ p_rings }}{{ p_knowledge }}{{ p_bar }}{{ p_glossary }}{{ p_rings }}{{ p_pair }}{{ p_feature }}{{ p_continue }}
  {%- else -%}
    {{ p_hero }}{{ p_intro }}{{ p_pair }}{{ p_archive }}{{ p_glossary }}{{ p_feature }}{{ p_continue }}
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "HA — The Masters page",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "ha-section-wrapper",
  "max_blocks": 20,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The Masters (Aloha's build brief and the founder's artboard, 18 Sept 2026). Add one Technique block per glossary entry, in order, and up to three Archive blocks for the small images above the quotation." },
    { "type": "select", "id": "ink", "label": "Heading ink", "default": "resin", "options": [
      { "value": "resin", "label": "Cutch Resin (as the artboard draws it)" },
      { "value": "peat", "label": "Peat (as the Clothing pages)" }
    ], "info": "Confirm against the editable artwork — the brief says not to assume the Clothing colour applies here." },
    { "type": "select", "id": "layout", "label": "Layout", "default": "brief", "options": [
      { "value": "brief", "label": "18 September (the build brief)" },
      { "value": "sep26", "label": "26 September (Aloha's new order)" }
    ], "info": "26 September: the quotation and MADE BY MASTERS on the paper, the knowledge band with swatches and her collage, ring bars between." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "start_muted", "label": "Films start muted (sound on request)", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "transcript_label", "label": "Transcript disclosure reads", "default": "Transcript" },
